A||||9||87FieroGTx||3.4 Turbo||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||06-23-2001||03:01 PM|||| I just picked up a 3.4 from a Firebird its in good shape it only has 27k. <P> Will the 2.8 Turbo work with it?<P> What kind of power does a stock (95?) 3.4 make?<P> If this works I'm going to put it in my 85 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||06-23-2001||04:03 PM||||If you strip the 2.8 and transfer everything to the 3.4 it will work.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||06-23-2001||05:41 PM||||The stock 3.4 from an F- body makes 160 horsepower. It depends on the turbo you use and what else you do to the engine but expect about 225-240 horsepower to start with.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87FieroGTx||06-23-2001||06:09 PM||||Thx guys) <P> I'v been looking around and I think I can git 220hp prob more out of the 3.4 befor adding the turbo so 220hp + 80hp = 300hp<P> Sounds good to me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Now all I need is a litle more $$$$ If everything goes as planned I should have it together by next summer.<P> Oh another question can you bore out or stroke a 3.4?||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-23-2001||10:11 PM||||You can bore the 3.4-liter engine but if your going to add a turbocharger than you want to bore it as little as possible. The 3.310 crankshaft stroke is about all your going to get.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||87FieroGTx||06-25-2001||08:20 PM|||| One last Question?<P> I have a Auto Trans will the turbo 3.4 be able to make any power using the auto? Can you change the shift points of the Auto? Or should I swap in a 4/5 Speed?<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||06-25-2001||08:30 PM||||I guess it depends on how you drive your Fiero. I'm on my 2nd auto tranny with a turbo 2.8<BR>The guy I bought it from abused it for a month or so, destroyed the tranny, and cracked the front manifold. The tranny in now is from a '88 Formula. I don't drive it hard, though I do get on it every once in a while <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, and I've had no problems.<BR>As far as the shift points, I don't know, but my mechanic would do something to make the tranny shift at a higher RPM. <P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||06-25-2001||11:15 PM||||I've read about a few guys that have tryed<BR>to use a turbo with 9.0:1 comp. in a Fiero<BR>that have crushed the second piston landing on one of the pistons!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>It's the hot running piston, can't remember which one that was.<BR>If you're still going to try it then you might want to do one or more of the following<BR>Turn the boost down to 6psi or less, use a<BR>timing retard device (MSD or Jacobs makes them), use an intercooler, adj. fuel regulator, use 8.5:1 or less comp. forged pistons, or use a water injection unit.<P>Here's the web-site of someone who already did a turbo 3.4:  <BR>http:members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||EdsB52||06-25-2001||11:51 PM||||Awesome web site Dave. That might be the best way to go for an engine upgrade. The engine fits easily, doesn't change weight or geometry, and produces gobs of HP. Only dig is the slight lag.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||06-26-2001||12:15 PM||||Oops I forgot some slashes in the web address.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>3.4 turbo web-site is: <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
